      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I hear how exhausting it feels to know the \"plot\" of your life is no longer entering, and I want you to know that believing your purpose is fully finished is a sense of loss that can feel very real. However, even when a major chapter ends, there is often a quiet space where new, unexpected stories can begin, even if they feel small or uncertain for now. You are not haunting your life by feeling this end; you are simply navigating the necessary grief of a transition that is very painful but not irreversible.",
